From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 12:00:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: build the nvkvm-broker display relay

One more file in the list patch 0001 introduced.  It implements
-display nvkvm-broker: connect to the broker's unix socket, relay the
guest's scanout dma-buf fd onward with SCM_RIGHTS, and feed the input
events that come back into qemu_input_*.

It is a deliberately small file, and it adds NO new build dependency:
there is no libdrm, no EGL and no GL in it, because in broker mode QEMU
imports nothing.  The import happens in the compositor or the X server,
one process out, from a descriptor QEMU merely forwarded.

Note the file is gated on CONFIG_LINUX and NOT on CONFIG_OPENGL.  That
is load-bearing: nvkvm_present_egl.c is compiled under
`#if defined(CONFIG_OPENGL) && NVKVM_QEMU_GRAPHICS`, so putting the
relay there would mean --disable-opengl compiles the display path away
entirely -- in the one configuration broker mode exists to make
possible.

Applies on top of 0001, which created the file list.
---
diff --git a/hw/misc/meson.build b/hw/misc/meson.build
index ef97efc..8039450 100644
--- a/hw/misc/meson.build
+++ b/hw/misc/meson.build
@@ -166,5 +166,6 @@ system_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_VIRTIO'], if_true: files(
   'nvkvm_isolate_handlers.c',
   'nvkvm_tables.c',
   'nvkvm_present_egl.c',
+  'nvkvm_display_relay.c',
 ))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_LASI', if_true: files('lasi.c'))
